# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Yuge Hu et al. (2022). Robust and scalable uncertainty estimation with conformal prediction for machine-learned interatomic potentials.
#   Machine Learning Science and Technology. doi:10.1088/2632-2153/aca7b1  arXiv:2208.08337v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2208.08337v2 (sha256 bb05779cd4429af8...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 196 (Training/reliability). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
#
# Encoding scope: bibliographic facts only. The paper applies conformal
# prediction with latent-space distances to estimate system-level energy
# uncertainties of neural network force fields (GMP + SingleNN models on
# MD17 aspirin, QM9 and a 1M subset of OC20, and a pretrained GemNet-OC)
# and compares calibration and sharpness with ensembles, dropout and
# negative-log-likelihood models. Its results are uncertainty metrics,
# not accuracy metrics of a potential. Read from the arXiv preprint (v2).

